      "question": "What does this sequence most likely indicate?",
      "context": "02:09-02:11 EventID=4625 TargetUserName=admin IpAddress=203.0.113.50 LogonType=3 (38 events)\n02:12:41 EventID=4624 TargetUserName=admin IpAddress=203.0.113.50 LogonType=3",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "Repeated network logon failures followed by a success from the same IP, consistent with password guessing"
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "A user mistyping a password once"
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "Kerberos ticket expiry"
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "A scheduled task starting"
        }
      ],
      "answer": [
        "a"
      ],
      "explanation": {
        "correct": "38 failed network logons (4625) then a success (4624) from one address is the classic guessing pattern.",
        "distractors": {
          "b": "One mistyped password would not generate dozens of failures.",
          "c": "Ticket expiry does not produce 4625 bursts from a remote IP.",
          "d": "Scheduled tasks log as different events."
        }
      }
